		{"id":"32830a0feb2ccc07","x":-640,"y":-720,"width":520,"height":60,"color":"1","type":"text","text":"# Excel for developers"},
		{
			"id":"29d06c7d0474467b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Why excel? \n\n- In 1982 Lotus 1-2-3, an electronic spreadsheet that became the best-selling personal-computer software of its day. \n- Microsoft Excel was first released in **1985**, initially for the Apple Macintosh. The Windows version followed in **1987**.\n- VBA (Visual Basic for Applications) was added to Excel in **1993**, with the release of **Excel 5.0**. \n\n**The problem of the chicken and the egg**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-640,
			"y":320,
			"width":520,
			"height":340,
			"color":"3"
		}
	],
